# Code ownership (botforge — source of truth).
# The ruleset on main requires a code-owner review (1 approval); this file
# maps every path to its owner. Mod rule/environment docs are owned by the
# mod's game designer; governance, conventions and sync scripts stay
# maintainer-owned.

## Default: a maintainer reviews everything not explicitly delegated
*                       @jj-guild/maintainers

## Mod docs & rules: owned by the mod's designer — mod-only changes never
# require a maintainer review; each mod is delegated by one explicit line
# (added in the mod's own bootstrap PR).
/docs/MODS/kingdoms/     @Drasahaoe
/docs/MODS/marriage/    @Drasahaoe
# Default mod ownership: unclaimed mods belong to Merlin (the platform
# developer) until a designer claims them — the roster 'owns' column and
# this file stay in sync (contributors-sync ownership check)
/docs/MODS/ladder/     @merlin-pinpin
/docs/MODS/register/   @merlin-pinpin

## Governance and process docs
/AGENTS.md              @jj-guild/maintainers
/docs/DECISIONS/        @jj-guild/maintainers

## CI/CD workflows: the sync and validation machinery — maintainer-only,
## symmetric with botforge-services and botforge-infra
/.github/workflows/    @jj-guild/maintainers

## Sync and workflow scripts: they regenerate generated/, drive the roster
## gates and the authority matrix — maintainer-only, CODEOWNERS-protected
## under the workflows path
/scripts/               @jj-guild/maintainers

## Contributors roster: the source of truth for roles and teams
/CONTRIBUTORS.md      @jj-guild/maintainers
